      "answer": "- In each query select a static value that identifies where the row came from, and give it the same alias in every query.\\n- SELECT 'Orders' AS source_table, orderid\\n- FROM Sales.Orders\\n- UNION\\n- SELECT 'OrdersArchive' AS source_table, orderid\\n- FROM Sales.OrdersArchive\\n- ORDER BY orderid, source_table\\n- more:\\n  - The literal becomes a real column in the result, so it can be sorted and filtered like any other.\\n  - Keep the alias identical in both queries - the first query names the columns for the whole result, so a mismatch quietly hides which side a row came from.",
